Chapter: BytesToText2F

 The ARM64 web server routed `/api/health` as `napinhealth`: every 0x2F
 arrived correct on the wire and came out of the guest as 0x6E. This is the
 smallest program that shows it. The same source runs on both lanes and
 x86-64 is the oracle, so a disagreement between the two answers is the
 defect and no expected file has to encode which one is right.

 0x2F is the subject. 0x61 and 0x68 ride along because a fault that moved
 every byte would be a different bug from one that moves only the slash.

Section: Entry

  probe-bytes : List Integer = [47, 97, 112, 105, 47, 104]

  report : Integer -> Text
  report (x) =
   let t = unicode-bytes-to-text probe-bytes
   in "len=" & show (text-length t)
    & " cce0=" & show (char-code (char-at t 0))
    & " cce1=" & show (char-code (char-at t 1))
    & " cce4=" & show (char-code (char-at t 4))
    & " cce5=" & show (char-code (char-at t 5))
    & " roundtrip=" & show (list-at (text-to-unicode-bytes t) 0)
    & " text=" & t

  opening : [Console] Integer = act
    (print-line-uni (report 0))
    0
  end

